WEBVTT

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.430
What is it, Vidocq?

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:11.760
I've tested my hypothesis that explains

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.820
why Evolutionary Invasion Objects 
appeared on the Atlantic side,

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.830
and the route they took to get there.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:18.840
Oh...?

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:25.470
Their advance on Florida was the 
fruit of their failure in Taiwan,

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:30.360
and the Object that relayed news of 
that failure was this messenger.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:40.120
This is a visualization of data on marine creatures 
that may be carrying a messenger.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.500
I meticulously loaded all of 
it into my easy chair...

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:53.820
...and deduced every possible 
combination of what would eat what

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.760
and where they would go to find...

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.870
...every possible transmission route.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:06.300
However, even taking the shortest route,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.600
there is no way for them to get from 
Taiwan to Florida that quickly.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:11.490
Which means...

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.830
Yes. There must be some faster route 
we're not aware of yet.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.140
It's the reason an 
Evolutionary Invasion Object

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:23.640
slipped through our surveillance network 
and appeared the Atlantic Ocean.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.290
You don't mean...?!

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.520
An undersea tunnel.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:31.810
They're crossing via a tunnel underground

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:36.320
and getting to the Atlantic Ocean without 
detouring around any continents.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:38.040
Do you know where?

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:41.820
I know a few very likely spots.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:44.970
Let's get them investigated right away.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:51.140
Abilities of distinguished individuals, 
numerous throughout history,

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:53.400
have been stored in special E-genes.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.400
<b>E-genes</b>

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:57.500
The E-gene holders, 
who inherit those genes,

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.720
<b>AU balls</b>

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:02.800
summon the abilities sleeping 
within them via AU balls,

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:06.000
and embody AU weapons.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:12.170
The E-gene holders belonging to the 
supranational organization Dogoo

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:15.160
versus enemies from outer space 
known as Evolutionary Invasion Objects.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.530
This is the chronicle of their 
fateful battle for humanity!

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.890
Gun No. 8: Tunnel.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.250
<b>The Costa Rica seabed</b>

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:15.770
Bingo! There's a tunnel!

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.690
<b>The deck of the <i>C. Forrester</i> </b>

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.150
As I thought.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.800
Be careful. The thing that dug the 
hole might still be in there.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:23.950
Roger!

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:29.120
Geronimo!

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:31.130
Commander, allow me to 
make two corrections.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.500
Not "might be," but "are."

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:37.640
And not "the thing," but "the things."

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.090
<b>A girl who sleeps in </b>

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.390
What...

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:46.340
...mission did I come here on again?

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:47.720
Sio.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.490
A-A-Asao?!

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:51.950
Were you waiting?

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:53.940
Was I— what?

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:59.960
I-I-Isn't your swimsuit kinda too s-sexy?

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.100
<b>Bam </b>

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:57.520
<b>Tight </b>

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:59.520
<b>Bammm </b>

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:03.240
You think so? Yours is cute, too.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.400
What the—?! When did—?!

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.310
Shaddup. Jeez.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.190
This swimsuit is... 

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.600
Can you not just be quiet 
for a little while?

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.690
J-J-J-J-J-Jack?!

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:15.470
Oh, is this your boyfriend, Sio?

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:18.190
N-N-N-No!

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:19.840
Are you sure?

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.720
She's sure!

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.980
Besides, I have a proper lover.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:27.200
Isn't that right, Gandhi?

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.890
Sorry, Sio.

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:32.970
Sio, you're so cruel.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.290
Aren't I your real lover?

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:37.840
Nooo!

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:41.480
Oh, sure, different strokes and all.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:43.470
That's not it! Asao!

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:47.380
It's okay. I'll always be your friend.

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:50.210
Now, let's get our love to blossom.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:03.630
Oh, phew! Just a dream...

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:08.210
Morning.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:15.250
W-W-Why are you sleeping in my room?!

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:17.770
I was told to wake you up, Sio.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:22.750
We're having a meeting about our 
next mission over breakfast.

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:24.770
Oh! Okay.

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:29.000
But couldn't you just wake me up normally?

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:29.200
<b>I can't get used to these people...</b>

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:32.970
Princess, are you all right?

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:37.230
Fine. They're all numbers, no strength.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:40.090
More importantly, stay close to Europa.

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:40.870
Got it!

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:44.010
Bugs! So many legs!

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.410
Ugh, I hate creepy-crawlies!

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.590
Bugs...?

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.830
They've withdrawn into this hole.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:59.510
I see. Well, surface for the moment.

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:02.350
We've managed to confirm the 
existence of the tunnel.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:04.290
No. Let's check out the inside.

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:08.650
There's one other thing I've 
got to confirm right now.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:12.230
Okay. Cyx and I will cover Europa.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.930
You don't need me as a defender?

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:18.490
Gaudi, you stay here and keep 
our path of retreat open.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:23.730
We're disconnecting, so we'll just go 
as far as the oxygen in our tanks allows.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.110
Okay. Thanks.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:34.240
Why do we have to go back 
up the First Platoon?

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:38.560
Does Jack not get along with the 
guys from the First Platoon?

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:43.110
Yeah. They get along about like cats and dogs. 
He's especially bad with Geronimo...

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:43.810
Shaddup!

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:48.010
In the first place, they shouldn't 
need us if those guys are there.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.480
Don't be so sure.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:56.120
It sounds very likely that this undersea 
tunnel is an important enemy base.

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:59.820
You mean we haven't seen 
the most insane ones yet?

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:01.660
Maybe not...

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:07.080
Umm... where do new 
Invasion Objects come from?

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:08.750
What do you mean?

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:14.690
If the tunnel is an enemy base, I thought maybe 
some kind of secret could be hidden there...

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:16.580
Whadaya mean, "some kind of secret"?

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.390
Well, I don't have any specific ideas, but...

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:24.620
Any twerp off the street could tell 
you there's "some kind of secret."

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:29.960
Quit the worthless musing and focus on 
how to up your marksmanship.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:36.610
Well, I think Vidocq and the special team 
guys will be considering all of that, so...

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:40.930
All we're here to do is take out the 
Invasion Objects in front of us.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:45.800
Okay! Second Platoon, we're moving out.

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.640
Starting the drop pod ejection sequence!

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:08.450
Destination: Maritime Costa Rica.

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:12.980
Drop pod ejection preparations complete.

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:14.690
Ejecting now!

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:26.640
This isn't just a tunnel. 
There are a ton of caves.

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:29.910
Caves or... little rooms.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:31.890
Would you take a peek inside for me?

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:32.990
Roger!

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:37.320
Ugh! They're everywhere!

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:43.930
But it seems like they're protecting 
something. Wonder what...

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.310
What's that...?

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:48.900
Beginning analysi—

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:50.620
Miss Geronimo?!

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:53.110
Sorry, Vidocq. This is as far as we go.

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:54.210
What's wrong?

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:55.230
Princess?

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:56.680
I have a bad feeling.

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.030
Something's coming.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:01.170
Get us outta here, Cyx!

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.050
You got it!

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.200
Here it comes. Gaudi!

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:08.840
Yep!

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:13.200
We'll be at the exit in 30 seconds. 
The moment we pass, plug up the hole!

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.550
That, and make us a road to the surface!

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.080
Roger! I'm on it!

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:40.920
It's huge...

00:10:46.970 --> 00:10:48.460
Entering the battle zone momentarily.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:52.410
Galiko!

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:59.230
Please release her from the AU weapon. 
At this rate, the feedback to her body will—

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:00.470
No.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:05.070
If Galileo doesn't recover observation 
sphere Europa before they split,

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:07.650
the data we acquired will be lost.

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:09.060
That's a problem.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:13.670
Sorry, but you'll have to bear it until 
Europa is recovered, Galiko.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:14.750
Vidocq, you tyrant!

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.550
I need that data.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.610
I know. I'll do my best.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:26.920
Dammit! I...

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:28.730
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.050
The Second Platoon!

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:35.350
Catch, Hunter!

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:37.570
Galiko!

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:44.000
I recovered it, Mr. Vidocq...

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:47.290
You sure did. Nice work, Galiko.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:53.990
It's leaving?

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:56.890
Are you okay? Hey!

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:58.850
Medic, on the double! Please!

00:11:58.850 --> 00:11:59.520
Yessir! 

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:00.360
Treat her immediately!

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:01.240
Hurry up! 

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:04.180
Please output this ball's data 
as soon as possible.

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:04.730
Yessir!

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:06.490
Vidocq!

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.800
Galileo...

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:18.950
Was it... looking this way?

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:33.430
A battleship-class! 
It's lying low in the tunnel!

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:36.280
Please stay on the lookout.

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:36.940
Sir.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:40.260
Galiko! Galiko!

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:41.400
Galileo!

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.640
Stay back, you guys.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:46.810
Thanks, Nobunagun.

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:52.130
Not at all. Galileo's our friend, right? 
I'm worried about her.

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:55.470
And then there's that bastard Vidocq.

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:59.300
Doesn't even show his face— 
is the analysis that important?!

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.900
The commander sure is a worrywort.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:07.090
The First Platoon would've been plenty.

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:10.790
Huh? I got the feeling that squid bastard 
was giving you some trouble.

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.560
Was I just seeing things?

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:17.660
I don't want to hear that from the guy 
who just swipes all the fun bits.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:19.270
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.660
I'm back.

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:25.210
What's up? Why the hostile vibes?

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:29.340
Oh, good! So this is your first time 
meeting the First Platoon, huh?

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:30.350
Ah— yes.

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:32.300
In the middle is Geronimo.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:34.380
On the right is Cyx.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.230
And on the left is Gaudi.

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:39.360
Ah! Nice to meet you!

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:41.120
O-Ogura Sio...

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:44.960
Er... I'm Nobunagun. Nice to meet you.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:50.460
All I ask is that you take care not 
to get in the princess's way.

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:52.460
I... I'll try not to!

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:54.570
That's so weird...

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:56.090
Umm... Gaudi...

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:58.940
What have you been 
looking at all this time?

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.270
Ah! Nothing! Nothing at all!

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:05.000
Grown-ups are... so mean...!

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:05.030
<b>'Shopped </b>

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:05.030
<b>Reality </b>

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:06.630
Oh. Vidocq.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:08.830
Oh! Wait up, Vidocq!

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:11.480
Something I can do for you, Nobunagun?

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:16.660
I have a favor to ask. 
Would you please go visit Galileo?

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:17.500
Why?

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:22.640
I think, if you went to see her, 
it would make her feel much better.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.920
Even if you just dropped by 
for a little while...

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.380
Don't be ridiculous.

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:27.040
Huh?

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:29.480
I don't have time for that.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:32.090
What? But that's so cold!

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:35.710
Will visiting Galiko improve 
our current state of affairs?

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:41.180
What we need to prioritize is analyzing 
and defeating the Invasion Object.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:43.730
I'm sure you could spare a little time.

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.180
Hunter!

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:47.470
You're gonna tell me the same thing?

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:51.570
You saw Galiko practically killing 
herself for you, right?

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:54.510
This and that are two different issues.

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:57.130
I have things I need to do.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:58.540
Hey, get back here!

00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:01.940
It's not like he's wrong.

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:02.770
What?

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:08.070
Heading into battle, you might get hurt, 
and if you screw up, you die.

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:12.760
Galiko did the job she had to do 
and got hurt. That's it.

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:14.820
That might be true, but—!

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:18.390
Saying shit like that is why 
you'll always be a squirt!

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:22.420
C'mon, guys, calm down.

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:24.760
There's no point in fighting here.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:28.910
Newb, quit worrying about everyone else 
and worry about yourself.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.540
If you don't want to die, that is.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:34.830
That's right. And whatever you 
Second Platooners do, don't get in our way.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:36.930
We're not gonna get screwed 
'cause of you guys.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.300
The hell?!

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:41.520
Talk about cold-blooded jerks!

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:45.540
No, I agree. It's natural to 
worry about your friends.

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:48.680
Oh? Disagreeing with us?

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.350
Look at you!

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:53.660
Getting all spunky because 
there's a new girl!

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.450
That's not it at all...

00:15:58.610 --> 00:15:59.910
Commander?!

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:00.590
Why...?

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:05.120
I'll be taking direct command 
of the next operation.

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:09.580
Meaning she will be in command 
in person on the ground.

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:12.370
I'd like you to understand 
the significance of this.

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:18.590
So that's how important 
this battle will be?

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:24.140
The First and Second Platoons 
will run a joint operation

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:30.110
to take out the battleship-class 
Evolutionary Invasion Object!

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:46.650
It really is big, isn't it?

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.400
Oh? Losing your nerve?

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:51.000
Don't make me laugh.

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:55.230
I won't let Galileo's hard work be in vain!

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:06.640
We have a full view of the 
Invasion Object via sonar.

00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:09.760
Enemy identified as a 
cephalopod-like Invasion Object.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:11.860
It has two tentacles capable of attacking.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:16.820
In order to damage the body, 
we'll have to disable those tentacles.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:19.690
Looking from here, 
the First Platoon will take the left one,

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:21.780
and the Second Platoon will take the right.

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:23.810
Begin the operation.

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:26.860
Gaudi!

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:27.600
Got it!

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:31.430
Let's do it!

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:33.010
Okay, Princess!

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:37.070
We'll be up ahead!

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:40.020
Wait for me!

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:43.530
The hell are you doing? 
We're goin' ahead, Squirt!

00:17:43.530 --> 00:17:46.030
Whaaaat?! Don't leave me here!

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:49.020
Cyx!

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:50.450
Roger!

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:53.900
First!

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:58.920
You're pretty full of yourself 
for an octopus.

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:01.320
Eat dirt!

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:06.110
It doesn't have any bones!

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:13.770
Made it!

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:14.930
You're late!

00:18:14.930 --> 00:18:16.260
I'm sorry!

00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:20.870
All right!

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:21.560
Watch out!

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.830
That thing's got bugs inside?!

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:32.400
Landmine-class ones that 
explode on impact, at that!

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.390
Newton, step on Squiddy 
so he can't go wild.

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:47.530
Nobunagun and I will attack from 
behind Gandhi's barrier.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:51.930
We'll clean up the bugs 
as we close in on the squid bastard!

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:53.340
Who put you in charge?!

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:54.940
Don't say "barrier"!

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:56.400
Shaddup! Let's move!

00:18:57.330 --> 00:19:00.880
Everyone is used to combat. 
I gotta do my best, too.

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:10.180
The First Platoon is so far away.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:14.400
While we've been fighting, 
the arms on the sides have opened up...

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:25.050
No... those showy tentacles are just 
drawing our battle focus! Its real aim is...

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:29.470
...the completely deserted <i>Clayton Forrester!</i>

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.830
Nobody's realized this?!

00:19:33.950 --> 00:19:36.470
What should I do? What can I do?

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:38.490
Newton!

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:41.130
She could release the extra gravity and 
change the angle of the enemy...

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.530
Huh? Did you say something?

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.200
Uh... umm...

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:46.430
Gandhi!

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:49.260
He could put up a barrier blocking 
the enemy's entire body...

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:52.180
What? I'm kinda busy. Make it quick!

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:54.860
Uh... it's... never mind.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.990
What should I do? 
It's just a feeling, anyhow.

00:19:57.990 --> 00:20:00.490
We've all got 
our own battles to fight.

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:03.400
And they're all more 
used to combat than me.

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:07.840
Persuade them? But I don't have time. 
Isn't there anything else...?

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:12.270
It can't be helped!

00:20:13.700 --> 00:20:15.200
The battleship is surfacing!

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:23.910
It shot!

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:24.780
It's huge!

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:26.170
Is that a landmine, too?

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:27.550
If it is...

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:29.420
Crap! It's heading right for...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:30.830
...the commander!

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.010
Evasive maneuvers!

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:34.290
It's no use! We won't make it in time!

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:39.380
When did she—?!

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:41.050
Yes! Shoot it down!

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:44.830
No! It's too close. 
If she blows it up there, we'll all...

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:19.440
If that had made a direct hit...

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:21.580
Man, I hadn't even noticed...

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:23.590
That new recruit...

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:24.580
No kidding.

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:27.980
And the <i>Clayton Forrester?</i>

00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:31.510
Ma'am! There is no damage 
to the engine. We can sail.

00:21:34.780 --> 00:21:36.550
Calling all holders.

00:21:36.550 --> 00:21:40.490
Suspend combat operations and 
return to the <i>Clayton Forrester.</i>

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:43.150
We will withdraw temporarily 
to restrategize.

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:46.130
I repeat: we will withdraw temporarily.

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:27.130
Sio, I watched <i>Gamera!</i>

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:27.760
How was it?

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:32.300
There was a monster like a knife and 
an alien like a squid— pretty cool!

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:34.090
No! That's not it, Asao...

00:23:34.740 --> 00:23:37.240
Next time, Gun No. 9: Sio and Kaoru!

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:39.090
I'll be the one to protect Sio!
